{"ld": 1548, "paper": "SP632", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Prevent the Introduction or Transfer of Invasive Fish Species in Inland Waters of the State", "sponsor_id": "s-black-russell", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-mason-richard", "h-thorne-james", "h-wood-stephen"], "committee_code": "IFW", "committee_name": "Inland Fisheries and Wildlife", "summary": {"text": "This bill increases the suspension and revocation of a fishing license from 5 years to 10 years for the following 3 offenses: failing to acquire a permit to import live freshwater fish or eggs except for live baitfish or smelts, to stock inland waters and to import live fish taken within the State. It reduces the mandatory suspension of a fishing license for the violation of illegal possession of live fish from 5 years to one year.\n\nIt adds mandatory restitution for failing to acquire a permit to stock inland waters and failing to acquire a permit to introduce fish or fish eggs into a private pond, and the court must order an offender to pay the Department of Inland Fisheries and Wildlife an amount equal to the cost of labor, equipment, chemicals and all other related expenses directly associated with mitigating or reclaiming waters affected as a result of a violation and direct the offender to provide the Commissioner of Inland Fisheries and Wildlife proof of that payment.\n\nCurrent law requires a permit to transport live fish for breeding and advertising. The bill eliminates the specific activities of breeding and advertising so the permit is required more generally for transport of live fish except for live baitfish and smelts taken within the State.\n\nThe bill creates a prohibition for disposal of live baitfish or smelts into inland waters, which is a civil violation. It also changes references to gametes and fish spawn to fish eggs.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0632&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Enacted", "final_disposition": {"label": "Enacted", "date": "2025-06-17", "governor_action": "Signed", "governor_action_date": "2025-06-17"}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1548)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0632&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (S-312)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0632&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}], "amendments": [{"id": "C-A (S-312)", "description": null, "sponsor": null, "status": "Adopted by House & Senate", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0632&item=2&snum=132", "fiscal_note_url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/bills_132nd/fiscalpdfs/FN154802.pdf"}], "committee_actions": [{"date": "2025-05-05", "action": "Work Session Held", "result": null}, {"date": "2025-05-05", "action": "Voted", "result": "OTP-AM"}, {"date": "2025-06-06", "action": "Reported Out", "result": "OTP-AM"}], "committee_reports": [{"label": "Committee report", "recommendation": "Ought to Pass as Amended", "signer_count": null, "signers": [], "signer_ids": []}], "chamber_actions": [{"date": "2025-04-10", "chamber": "Senate", "action": "Committee on INLAND FISHERIES AND WILDLIFE suggested and ordered printed REFERENCE to the Committee on INLAND FISHERIES AND WILDLIFE Ordered sent down forthwith for concurrence"}, {"date": "2025-04-10", "chamber": "House", "action": "The Bill was REFERRED to the Committee on INLAND FISHERIES AND WILDLIFE."}, {"date": "2025-04-10", "chamber": "House", "action": "In concurrence. ORDERED SENT FORTHWITH."}, {"date": "2025-05-05", "chamber": "J", "action": "Work Session Held"}, {"date": "2025-05-05", "chamber": "J", "action": "Voted: OTP-AM"}, {"date": "2025-06-06", "chamber": "J", "action": "Reported Out: OTP-AM"}, {"date": "2025-06-09", "chamber": "Senate", "action": "Report READ and ACCEPTED."}, {"date": "2025-06-09", "chamber": "Senate", "action": "READ ON